# Renode deterministic tick-mode regression (ARM / Cortex-M).
#
# Deterministic-time lockstep variant of stm32f103_smoke: the fixture
# sets tick_mode, so klippy's reactor advances simulated time only via
# `advance T` round-trips over the launcher's tick socket, and the
# launcher drives Renode with `emulation RunFor` + a synchronous
# USART1<->pty byte shuttle (renode_hooks.serial_write_hex / RunFor /
# serial_drain_hex). This removes the wall-clock-vs-virtual-time drift
# the free-running (non-tick) Renode path suffers from.
#
# This used to mis-frame identify ("Unknown message -16"): the launcher's
# monitor round-trips were delimited by matching Renode's `(<context>)`
# prompt, which an echoed command containing a parenthesised identifier
# could satisfy mid-chunk, desyncing every subsequent round-trip and
# corrupting the byte shuttle. The sentinel-delimited _send_monitor
# (renode_launcher.py) fixed that, and single-MCU ARM tick mode now
# passes reliably on a clean host. (Multi-renode tick lockstep is still
# flaky under host contention; the simavr/AVR tick path still needs a
# synchronous shuttle - see emulator_tick_mode.test.)
DICTIONARY stm32f103.dict
CONFIG stm32f103_smoke.cfg
EMULATOR stm32f103_tick.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
